									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lightvsdark777" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1928087); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1928087&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605900850" alt="Lightvsdark777" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1928087)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/lightvsdark777" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1928087); return false;" >Lightvsdark777</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605899969 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Nov 2020 19:19</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13868913/the-spider-queen-first-scp">The Spider Queen (First SCP)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823945">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Not yet.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> haven't settled on one yet</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A Euclid-class queen of spiders that was saddened by humanity's cruelty towards her children to the point where her heart literally cracked. Because of this, she's surprisingly passive. She can make new species of spiders (both normal and anomalous) at will, and spiders flock to her.</p>
<p><strong>Narrative Pitch:</strong> Though she has waged several wars against humanity in the past due to the mistreatment of her children that got fiercer as time went on, her heart eventually cracked, flushing all hatred from her body in a single moment. All that was left behind was sorrow. Sorrow for her fallen children, and sorrow for sending her children to die in who knows how many wars that they never won. So she packed her things and left the mainland, retreating to an island. Many, many years later, the foundation responds to a radio signal from a battleship claiming that they were being attacked by an enormous spider. It's revealed that she created this spider as a guardian for her personal island that she sends out if she senses that people with bad intentions are coming to her island. The foundation does its thing, making the island as secret as possible while trying to study the spider queen. Eventually, the foundation manages to conduct some interviews with her.</p>
<p><strong>Hook:</strong> Aside from the aforementioned interviews, which reveal her backstory, this SCP should be interesting among the other spider-based SCPs that she's not immediately hostile to people. There should also be implications that some of the spider-based SCPs the foundation keeps tabs on are relics of these ancient wars fought by her.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> While she has potential, I want to hear your input for how I could improve her concept.</p>

							</div>

								
					
