														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823938">
									

<p><a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/deathbygin-2">http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/deathbygin-2</a></p>
<p>A short tale for my authored article SCP-5118.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoiler&nbsp;/&nbsp;Explanation</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Minimize</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>As Dr. Atmos gather information from Dr. Williams, it's implied that SCP-5118 is actually a dog who is a reality bender, turned human, and turned back into a dog when about to be captured. Evidence to support this includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>SCP-5118 did not act like most other reality benders do when discovering they have powers (usually by hiding them from others).</li>
<li>SCP-5118 manifests chocolate, grapes, and soda - all things a dog cannot eat.</li>
<li>SCP-5118 appeared to be smiling while being chased.</li>
<li>SCP-5118 does not attempt to breach containment because it's current living situation is already ideal (it gets a bed, new toys, guaranteed food and water, and socializes with staff daily when they provide it with food).</li>
<li>Using it's powers while in containment would risk exposing itself. Since it's implied that it's &quot;original form&quot; is already a dog, the scans / tests from the SCP article would show nothing.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I wanted to write this tale to add a twist to the article without making this the clear-cut canon. Please let me know what you think.</p>

							</div>

								
					
