														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823934">
									

<p>It's definitely has a more structured narrative now! But the whole setup of interviewing the anomaly and then she drops some important information (amidst a backstory about shadowy kidnappers) seems constructed, and more importantly, lacking in conflict. There aren't really stakes involved here that make this reveal dramatic. I encourage you to also implement a more standard, uh, rising-action/climax format as well.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After interviews with SCP-XXXX and observations in her character, Foundation researchers begin to believe that SCP-XXXX may be in fact Elaine of Astolat, also known as The Lady of Shallot from Alfred Tennyson famous poem.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I meant to bring this up, but how involved is this reference going to be? It seems like a throwaway atm, with no purpose but gesturing towards a popular poem as an inspiration. Is there some story going on about her being Tennyson's inspiration?</p>

