					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ancient-five" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5089398); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5089398&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605900850" alt="Ancient Five" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5089398)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ancient-five" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5089398); return false;" >Ancient Five</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605894298 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Nov 2020 17:44</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13868618/irish-fairies">Irish Fairies</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823885">
									

<p>Hey! Not a greenlighter, sorry.</p>
<p>So, your object itself is interesting enough- a nice cultural reference is generally good, and you also changed it up a little so that it wasn't just pulling straight from stories that already exist. Overall, the anomaly is solid enough, so that's good.</p>
<p>Your narrative is interesting. I enjoy the idea of a mysterious location like this one that represents a lot of danger for the Foundation, but if you leave it where you're leaving it now, the ending might be regarded as having too little detail. This seems like something that would be explored more than once, albeit with more appropriate gear the second time (for things like cognitohazards). Or, you could use drone exploration, if that would work. Really, I just think that you should either shine some light on this &quot;festival&quot; or at least provide some insight as to why they're saying &quot;come to the festival.&quot; If you intend to leave the reader with a lot of questions, you should get them a little closer to their answers so that they can infer details, rather than leaving it completely vague.</p>
<p>This type of object seems like the kind of thing that the Foundation is going to have a hard time containing- a sort of &quot;neutralize the threat by any means&quot; type of scenario. Do you plan on expanding on that through the narrative? That would definitely involve more exploration logs/action scenarios and stuff along those lines. I recommend including those types of things if that's the storyline you want to use, but if these are easy to contain, then I would instead suggest controlled experiments and research logs. In the end, though, you should do whatever you feel is best for the article and go from there- these are just suggestions.</p>
<p>Overall, the concept looks good. Try to get some additional advice on how to develop this narrative if you feel like you need it. I hope I was able to help. Good luck developing your idea!</p>

							</div>

								
					
